<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <%- include('partials/favicon') %>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover">
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= asset('/theme.css') %>">
  <%- include('partials/dialog') %>
  <style>
    .tools-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap:18px; }
    .tool-card { background:#111; border:1px solid #1e1e1e; border-radius:14px; padding:22px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:12px; }
    .tool-card h3 { margin:0; color:#e8e8e8; }
    .tool-card p { color:#777; line-height:1.6; min-height:72px; }
    .tool-meta { color:#555; font-size:0.75rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.08em; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>

<div class="container" style="padding-top:24px">
  <div style="max-width:760px;margin-bottom:24px">
    <h2 style="margin-bottom:8px">Tools</h2>
    <p>Operational tools and guided utilities live here. Timers are the first moved into this section, and the rest of the training helpers can expand here without cluttering the top nav.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="tools-grid">
    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Training Utility</div>
      <h3>⏱ Timers</h3>
      <p>Round timer, interval timer, EMOM, AMRAP, stopwatch, combo caller, and a tempo clock. Tap + on a timer to save that setup on your account. The stopwatch is the one without a saved setup.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/timers">Open Timers</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Recovery Utility</div>
      <h3>🧘 Stretch Builder</h3>
      <p>Create warmup, cooldown, and mobility flows from exercise cards. Use it to build reusable prep and recovery routines just like saved workouts.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/stretch">Open Stretch</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Planning Utility</div>
      <h3>📋 Training Plans</h3>
      <p>View assigned plans, phase structure, and scheduled sessions. This stays available as a tool even while the top-level nav is simplified.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/plans">Open Plans</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Consistency Utility</div>
      <h3>🔥 Accountability</h3>
      <p>Review recent consistency, streaks, and session follow-through so the tools section also includes performance management, not just clocks.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/accountability">Open Accountability</a>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Calisthenics</div>
      <h3>🌳 Skill Tree</h3>
      <p>Bodyweight skills with prerequisites, from wall plank to freestanding handstand. Log attempts and unlock what comes next, based on the equipment you have.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/skills">Open Skill Tree</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Testing</div>
      <h3>📏 Fitness Tests</h3>
      <p>Calisthenics and general fitness tests with instructions. Results are kept over time and compared with your own earlier results.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/tests">Open Tests</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Cardio</div>
      <h3>🏃 Treadmill Test</h3>
      <p>A progressive treadmill test with tones and spoken speed cues, or a 12-minute distance test. Saves your last stage or distance.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/tests/treadmill">Open Treadmill Test</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Weekly</div>
      <h3>📈 Benchmarks</h3>
      <p>The movements you re-test every week: trends, your editable list, the weekly plan and the bot reminder.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/benchmarks">Open Benchmarks</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Equipment</div>
      <h3>🪜 Agility ladder</h3>
      <p>A collapsible ladder you design in the browser. Rails and rungs can each be paracord, printed bars, or dowels you cut. Download the parts sized for your printer, including a Bambu A1 mini.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/ladder">Open Ladder</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Equipment</div>
      <h3>Jump-rope handles</h3>
      <p>Two printed pieces and a length of paracord. A cap holds a double knot, and the handle screws into the cap on a large thread so the rope can be changed.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/rope">Open Jump Rope</a>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-card">
      <div class="tool-meta">Equipment</div>
      <h3>Landmine</h3>
      <p>A smooth ball that caps the end of a barbell. Set the ball size and the bar diameter, then download two pieces that screw together. Print it in PETG.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/landmine">Open Landmine</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>